From 0f790d77c0757f2f443e34090a388aef919e7237 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mark Hatle <mark.hatle@amd.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 19:42:33 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 7/8] qemu-system-amd-fpga-multiarch: Separate configure_versal
 into parts

detect_versal_boot_image now handles the boot mode processing for
versal and versal like machines.  This does require that the loader type
to be passed in.

setup_versal now handles the parsing and qemu configuration work.

The functions are called in a pattern similar to:

  multiboot_val = detect_versal_boot_image(known_args, drives, machine_path, VersalBootImageLoader)
  with VersalBootImageLoader(boot_pdi_path, 0) as loader:
      loader.parse()
      setup_versal(loader, known_args, unknown_args, machine_path, multiboot_val)

Upstream-Status: Pending

Signed-off-by: Mark Hatle <mark.hatle@amd.com>
